  "answer": "The knowledge base lists the following consequences of SQL Injection:\n\n1. **Unauthorized Access**: Attackers can gain unauthorized access to sensitive data within the database.\n2. **Data Manipulation**: Attackers may modify or delete data, leading to data integrity issues.\n3. **Data Exfiltration**: Sensitive information can be extracted from the database.\n4. **Denial of Service**: SQL Injection can be used to disrupt the normal functioning of the application, potentially leading to denial of service.\n5. **Compromise of Application Logic**: Attackers can manipulate the application's logic by altering SQL queries.\n\nThese consequences arise from the failure of the application to appropriately validate user input, allowing attackers to craft input that alters the intended SQL statements executed by the application [Source 1].",
